  "interpretation": [
    "The dev set favors lexical methods: character ranker and five hybrid configurations tie on dev MRR .975. The frozen tie order selects char4. Holdout is never used to choose among tied configurations.",
    "On unseen paired holdout, selected char4 loses one Top1 and places the gold below its opposite-direction/role/measure foil in four questions versus two for E5. MRR rises only .010833 while Top3 improves by two.",
    "On original paraphrase-heavy twelve, char4 falls to one Top1 versus six for E5. Neither synthetic holdout gains nor cheap latency justify replacing production E5.",
    "RRF and simple score fusion are inexpensive after E5 scores are available, but these remain development-only exploratory diagnostics under the frozen protocol. No extra neural model was justified or installed.",
    "The comparison holds all passages and candidate pools identical. It measures ranker differences and cannot credit improvements to the parents separate passage selection changes.",
    "All 40 new queries and 40 synthetic passages were authored before model calls. Labels remain exact issue/direction/speaker targets, not verified statements of law. Split questions are dependent within ten topic pairs; no claim of actual case retrieval or legal accuracy.",
    "The baseline scorer was pinned after an initial hash check blocked concurrent production changes before any holdout scoring. Initial and repeated dev metrics are exactly identical. Initial manifests and locked selection remain available for audit."
  ],
